$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: usm/pkg-universal-docs
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-28"
summary: >-
  Ship universal onboarding docs (getting-started, agent-setup-guide, per-editor MCP setup guides)
  inside the @smithgray/usm npm package and merge them into the consumer's generated docs tree when
  the consumer repo has no docs-source/ of its own. Consumer docs-source/ always wins; package
  content is fallback only.
$system: usm/system
$service: usm/cli
intent: >-
  A consumer installing @smithgray/usm into a fresh repo gets zero onboarding pages:
  getting-started, agent-setup-guide, and the per-editor MCP setup guides exist only in USM's own
  docs-source/, which the npm package does not ship. The docs homepage guard silently swaps the
  Getting Started link for "Browse the sidebar", so a new user's first click lands nowhere.
  Universal onboarding should come from the package itself and be merged into the consumer's
  generated docs when they have none of their own — the package knows how to teach USM; the
  consumer's docs shouldn't start empty. Also the carrier for issue #45's consumer guidance: version
  pinning, the upgrade → regenerate → commit workflow, and generate --check CI-gate semantics belong
  in shipped docs so every consumer agent inherits them instead of guessing in chat.
status: built
flows:
  - id: onboard-with-zero-setup
    name: Onboard with zero authored docs
    steps:
      - actor: adopter
        id: s1
        action: install
        surface: cli
        target: "@smithgray/usm in a repo that has no docs-source/ of its own"
      - actor: adopter
        id: s2
        action: run
        surface: cli
        target: usm generate
      - actor: adopter
        id: s3
        action: review
        surface: browser
        target: >-
          Getting Started and Agent Setup Guide pages in the docs preview — onboarding exists with
          zero authored content
      - actor: adopter
        id: s4
        action: follow
        surface: browser
        target: the agent-setup guide links into the per-editor MCP setup guides
  - id: consumer-override
    name: Override with your own docs-source
    steps:
      - actor: adopter
        id: s1
        action: create
        surface: spec
        target: docs-source/ in the repo root with their own agent-setup-guide.md or editor guides
      - actor: adopter
        id: s2
        action: run
        surface: cli
        target: usm generate
      - actor: adopter
        id: s3
        action: verify
        surface: browser
        target: their pages render and no package onboarding pages leaked in
  - id: merge-universal-docs
    name: Universal docs merge pipeline
    steps:
      - actor: agent
        id: s1
        action: detect
        target: consumer docs-source/ at the repo root
      - actor: agent
        id: s2
        action: copy
        target: consumer docs-source/ into the docs output tree when present (today's behavior, unchanged)
      - actor: agent
        id: s3
        action: resolve
        target: package docs-source/ when the consumer repo has none
      - actor: agent
        id: s4
        action: copy
        target: >-
          package universal pages into the docs output tree, skipping any filename that a generated
          page already claimed
contracts:
  - id: package-ships-universal-docs
    description: >-
      The npm package ships a universal docs-source/ directory with the onboarding pages every
      consumer repo needs; file list includes it so it lands in the tarball.
    must_have:
      - package files[] includes docs-source/
      - >-
        shipped set covers agent-setup-guide.md, getting-started.md, and editor-setup/ (index +
        per-editor guides)
      - shipped pages contain no repo-specific content (no Smith & Gray ids, no internal links)
  - id: consumer-override
    description: >-
      Precedence is total: consumer repo docs-source/ wins wholesale; generated reference_pages beat
      package content on filename collision; package content is fallback only.
    must_have:
      - >-
        consumer repo with docs-source/ gets byte-identical output to today (no package content
        copied)
      - consumer repo without docs-source/ gets the package set copied into the docs output tree
      - package file never overwrites a generated page with the same output name
      - merge is skipped in --check mode (no writes)
  - id: nav-lights-up-automatically
    description: >-
      Existing dead-link guards light up automatically once package content is present — no guard
      changes required for consumers to see onboarding nav.
    must_have:
      - homepage renders the Getting Started link when the package page was copied (hasPage guard)
      - >-
        sidebar shows Editor Setup and Agent Setup Guide entries when the pages exist (docExists
        guard)
      - consumer trees without the package content keep today's guarded behavior (no regression)
  - id: link-discipline-in-consumer-tree
    description: >-
      All shipped pages pass the full-link discipline in the CONSUMER output tree: every link
      resolves, sidebar and content, both docs audiences.
    must_have:
      - no relative or .md-suffixed hrefs in shipped page content
      - crawl of a consumer fixture tree: 0 dead links, 0 duplicate links, both audiences
      - >-
        cross-page links limited to pages guaranteed by the copy step (editor-setup/,
        agent-setup-guide, getting-started) or guarded at generation time
  - id: idempotent-universal-docs
    description: >-
      Package docs merge is deterministic and repeatable: same inputs produce byte-identical output
      trees.
    must_have:
      - second usm generate run produces byte-identical docs output
      - removed package files do not leave orphans in a clean tree
      - existing consumer-repo behavior unchanged for every other generator pass
tests:
  - id: consumer-without-docs-source
    setup:
      consumer_repo_fixture_without_docs_source: true
    expect:
      - assertion: agent-setup-guide.md and editor-setup/index.md exist in the docs output tree
      - assertion: sidebar contains Editor Setup and Agent Setup Guide entries
      - assertion: homepage shows the Getting Started link
    flow: onboard-with-zero-setup
  - id: consumer-with-docs-source
    setup:
      consumer_repo_fixture_with_docs_source: true
    expect:
      - assertion: consumer pages copied; package onboarding pages absent
      - assertion: output byte-identical to pre-feature generate run
    flow: consumer-override
  - id: link-crawl-consumer-tree
    setup:
      consumer_fixture_docs_built: true
    expect:
      - assertion: 0 dead links, 0 duplicate links across sidebar and content in both audiences
      - assertion: no relative or .md-suffixed hrefs in shipped pages
  - id: idempotent-merge
    setup:
      generate_run_twice: true
    expect:
      - assertion: second run byte-identical
      - assertion: "--check mode writes nothing"
see_also:
  - usm/cli-generate
  - usm/cli-docs
implementation:
  primary: >-
    src/cli/index.ts (Pass 0 docs-source copy); package.json files[]; docs-source/getting-started.md
    (new); docs-source/agent-setup-guide.md (link fixes); docs-source/editor-setup/* (absolute
    links)
  test_code: tests/packageDocs.test.ts
  test_code_status: manual
